{"availability":"available","full":"QuarkLangCommunity/QuarkLangQkc","name":"QuarkLangQkc","description":"QuarkLang — a type-first compiled language: Go interpreter + LLVM backend (qkc), with linter, doc generator, REPL and LSP. Zero third-party deps. 类型在前的中文友好编译型语言。","category":"Developer tools","language":"Go","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-29T12:35:53Z","updated":"2026-10-11T06:13:42Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://quarklangcommunity.github.io/QuarkLangQkc/","topics":["chinese","cli","compiler","interpreter","linter","llvm","lsp","programming-language","repl","static-analysis","tree-sitter","type-first","zero-dependencies"],"demo":"https://quarklangcommunity.github.io/QuarkLangQkc/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T06:14:15.614Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T06:14:15.614Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T06:14:15.614Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T06:14:15.614Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["QuarkLang is a type-first compiled language with two backends for one source file — a Go interpreter (edit and run) and an LLVM compiler qkc (performance on par with C). It targets compute-heavy, highly concurrent, allocation-heavy CLI and service workloads: fib(35) in 21 ms (C: 22 ms), Erlang-style user-space tasks, and a block allocator with no GC pauses. It ships with a linter, doc generator, REPL, language server and editor support — and zero third-party Go dependencies.","Everything in the GIF is real output (regenerate it with scripts/make-demo-gif.py): quark hello.qk → qkc -run hello.qk → QKLANG=en qkcheck examples/ (a genuine warning, not a mock-up). The last line demonstrates the bilingual tooling: the same command prints Chinese by default."],"features":["Compiled performance = C: same LLVM -O3 backend (fib35 21 ms vs C 22 ms; P99 latency on par at every quantile).","Erlang-style concurrency: spawn/merge/block/done/channel user-space tasks on a thread pool — Erlang's model with C-level performance.","Zero-GC memory: linear block allocation + an occupancy min-heap; delete returns blocks to the free queue (data preserved),","clear actually wipes them — no GC pauses, 0.195% fragmentation, 99.96% reuse.","Mathematical sum optimization: closed form for linear/periodic/uniform-random sums — 1e9 terms in O(1) (2 ms; a Go loop needs 223 ms)."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/QuarkLangCommunity/QuarkLangQkc/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"456e34cbf1966b489b926698d5049c853416c314e74807953280b4bede6e91cd","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T06:14:15.761Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T06:14:15.761Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"QuarkLang is a type-first compiled language with two backends for one source file — a Go interpreter (edit and run) and an LLVM compiler qkc (performance on par with C). It targets compute-heavy, highly concurrent, allocation-heavy CLI and service workloads: fib(35) in 21 ms (C: 22 ms), Erlang-style user-space tasks, and a block allocator with no GC pauses. It ships with a linter, doc generator, REPL, language server and editor support — and zero third-party Go dependencies.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/QuarkLangCommunity/QuarkLangQkc/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"456e34cbf1966b489b926698d5049c853416c314e74807953280b4bede6e91cd","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/QuarkLangCommunity/QuarkLangQkc/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T06:14:15.762Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-11T06:13:42Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/QuarkLangCommunity/QuarkLangQkc/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T06:14:15.763Z","hash":"456e34cbf1966b489b926698d5049c853416c314e74807953280b4bede6e91cd","originalBytes":34991,"storedBytes":34991,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["interpreter","examples","compiler","qkc","quark","int","qkcheck","lang","library","qklsp","run","language","qkrepl","tes